[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 746,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 576,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114913,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 335,
        "headingId": 576,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Segmental odontomaxillary dysplasia (SOD) is a non-hereditary unilateral developmental disorder characterized by segmental maxillary and soft tissue enlargement with dento-osseous abnormalities and occasionally homolateral cutaneous manifestations.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:09:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 747,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 577,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114914,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 335,
        "headingId": 577,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:09:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 748,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 578,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114915,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 335,
        "headingId": 578,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>DA07.3 Disturbances in tooth formation</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:09:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 749,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 579,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114916,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 335,
        "headingId": 579,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:09:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 750,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 580,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114917,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 335,
        "headingId": 580,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:09:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 751,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 581,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114918,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 335,
        "headingId": 581,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>SOD is a unilateral maxillary enlargement, occurring almost equally on the right or left side, in the premolar/molar region of the maxilla.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:09:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 752,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 582,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114919,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 335,
        "headingId": 582,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients present with a painless maxillary buccal and palatal enlargement, usually in the first or second decade of life, with a failure of tooth eruption and with dental abnormalities clinically and radiographically. Enlargement appears stable and non-progressive, starting in childhood and continuing until puberty. Frequently there is associated fibrous gingival hyperplasia {2371053}. The maxillary overgrowth extends to the sinus, reducing its volume radiographically {11027387}.</p>\r\n<p>Dental abnormalities include missing permanent teeth (usually premolars), retained primary molars beyond the normal time of exfoliation, enamel and dentine hypoplasia, and altered tooth shape and size. Facial manifestations, often subtle, include hypertrichosis, hyperpigmentation or hypopigmentation (including Becker naevus), an increased frequency of melanocytic naevi, erythema, and lip clefting {29389339; 32893658}.</p>\r\n<p>There is a poorly defined overlap of features with some related presentations and syndromes including hemimaxillofacial dysplasia {3477765} and HATS syndrome (hemimaxillofacial enlargement, asymmetry of the face, tooth abnormalities, and skin findings) {25372264}.</p>\r\n<h5>Imaging</h5>\r\n<p>Panoramic and periapical radiographs show a poorly defined area of abnormal bone, often with a characteristic vertical trabeculation, and coarse radiopacities.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:09:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 753,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 583,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114920,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 335,
        "headingId": 583,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>SOD is rare and has a slight male predilection.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:09:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 754,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 584,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114921,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 335,
        "headingId": 584,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The etiology is unknown. Proposed causes include prenatal trauma, endocrine abnormalities, and bacterial or viral infection.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:09:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 755,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 585,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114922,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 335,
        "headingId": 585,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The possibility that somatic <em>PIK3CA</em> or <em>ACTB</em> mutations contribute to the overgrowth has been raised {32500425}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:09:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 762,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 592,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114923,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 335,
        "headingId": 592,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Bone trephine or sample with tooth fragments</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:09:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 756,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 586,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114924,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 335,
        "headingId": 586,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Gingival biopsies may reveal fibrous hyperplasia with occasional dystrophic calcifications. Bone biopsies reveal irregular bone spicules with multiple accentuated reversal lines. The bone appears inert, without osteoblastic or osteoclastic activity, and histological features are probably the end stage of a much earlier developmental process. External root resorption of teeth, with dysplastic dentine and fibrosis of the pulp, has been described {29389339}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:09:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 757,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 587,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114925,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 335,
        "headingId": 587,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:09:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 758,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 588,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114926,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 335,
        "headingId": 588,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:09:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 761,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 591,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114927,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 335,
        "headingId": 591,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> localized swelling; abnormal soft tissues, bone, and teeth; characteristic radiographic features.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> inert bone histologically, with defects of tooth formation (only if fibrous dysplasia requires exclusion).</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:09:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 759,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 589,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114928,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 335,
        "headingId": 589,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:09:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 760,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 590,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114929,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 335,
        "headingId": 590,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>SOD shows slow or minimal enlargement until puberty. Surgery may be required for cosmetic and functional purposes.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:09:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]